        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: அனுமதி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அனுமதி (aṉumati) — \"permission\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Permission to do a thing — asked for, given, refused. Here all three sisters took the same Sanskrit word and did not even change its shape: Kannada ಅನುಮತಿ (anumati), Telugu అనుమతి (anumati), Tamil அனுமதி (aṉumati)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hold it apart from விடை, which you already have. விடை is permission to go, taken formally at a door. அனுமதி (aṉumati) is the wider one and covers everything else you might be allowed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "aṉumati",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *aṉumati*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "aṉumati, then viḍai, and say which of the two is only about leaving",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *aṉumati*, then *viḍai*, and say which of the two is only about leaving]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does அனுமதி (aṉumati) mean? (\"permission\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
