          "title": "You'll want to know: தயக்கம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தயக்கம் (tayakkam) — \"hesitancy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The holding back before you ask: the half-step not taken, the sentence begun and dropped. Kannada carries the same idea in ಸಂಕೋಚ (saṅkōca)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The தயவு inside தயவுசெய்து opens the same way and is a different word — that one is kindness given, this one is a foot kept back. Tamil puts them next to each other and expects you to hear the difference."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
